  ],
  "sourceEvidence": [
    {"id": "ATL105-2026-3-SEG100-E86", "sourcePage": 402, "startLine": 21458, "quote": "Number: 86 Name: Sequence Number\nCharacter Type: N Maximum Length: 6 bytes\nRepresentation: Fixed length of six digits\nPurpose: Note: Identifies a transaction for the life of the transaction.\nSequence Number must persist in all the subsequent transactions that are associated with the initial authorization request."},
    {"id": "ATL105-2026-3-SEG100-E86-RANGE", "sourcePage": 402, "startLine": 21487, "quote": "Valid Codes/Values: 000001–999999"},
    {"id": "ATL105-2026-3-SEG100-E86-PREAUTH-CAPTURE", "sourcePage": 402, "startLine": 21470, "quote": "In the case of a preauthorized transaction, the Sequence Number in the Purchase/Capture is the same Sequence Number as in the transaction’s Authorization Only request."},
    {"id": "ATL105-2026-3-SEG100-E86-REVERSAL", "sourcePage": 402, "startLine": 21473, "quote": "In the case of a purchase reversal/void or time-out reversal transaction, the Sequence Number must be the same as in the original transaction request."},
    {"id": "ATL105-2026-3-SEC10-1-2-2-AUTH-REVERSAL-APPROVAL", "sourcePage": "10.1.2.2", "startLine": 3957, "quote": "• Element No. 5 (Approval Number)—present in the original transaction—must be present and identical in the Authorization Only Reversal transaction."},
    {"id": "ATL105-2026-3-SEC10-1-2-2-AUTH-REVERSAL-SEQUENCE", "sourcePage": "10.1.2.2", "startLine": 3959, "quote": "• Element No.86 (Sequence Number)—present in the original transaction—must be present and identical in the Authorization Only Reversal transaction."},
    {"id": "ATL105-2026-3-SEC10-1-2-2-AUTH-REVERSAL-CODE", "sourcePage": "10.1.2.2", "startLine": 3961, "quote": "• Element No. 78 (Prompt Code) must contain a Transaction Type code “S” to indicate cancellation."},
    {"id": "ATL105-2026-3-SEC2-3-1-TOR-SEQUENCE", "sourcePage": "2.3.1", "startLine": 2009, "quote": "The Sequence Number, Account Number, and dollar amount—assigned by the customer’s host/controller/POS system—are the elements used to match a request with its respective response. The Sequence Number of a TOR must be the same as the Sequence Number of the financial transaction being reversed. Each time any financial transaction request is forwarded to BUYPASS, the financial transaction should be assigned a new Sequence Number by the customer’s host/controller/POS system."}
  ],
